From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:10:23 +0900
Subject: Output: update the mode list without a dangling iterator

A wl_output "current" mode event that repeats a known size and refresh rate removes the older
entry while an iterator to the new, last entry is kept. Since Qt 6 QList is an array: the erase
invalidates that iterator, the loop no longer stops at it and walks past the end. Compositors send
exactly that when an output's refresh rate or mode changes; plasmashell crashed in
Output::Mode::operator= (2026-09-27, display.mode/display.refresh acceptance, quick settings).
The list is walked by index up to the new last entry. Upstream master (2026-09-24) still has the
loop; 9affe9f only replaced the stored current-mode iterator.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-27
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [a plain bug; not fixed upstream as of 2026-09-24]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:display.refresh L3:recording.quicksetting
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/73
---
 src/client/output.cpp | 16 +++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/client/output.cpp b/src/client/output.cpp
index 79a2684..ebf7ee4 100644
--- a/src/client/output.cpp
+++ b/src/client/output.cpp
@@ -213,24 +213,26 @@ void Output::Private::addMode(uint32_t flags, int32_t width, int32_t height, int
     if (flags & WL_OUTPUT_MODE_PREFERRED) {
         mode.flags |= Mode::Flag::Preferred;
     }
-    auto currentIt = modes.insert(modes.end(), mode);
+    modes.append(mode);
     bool existing = false;
     if (flags & WL_OUTPUT_MODE_CURRENT) {
-        auto it = modes.begin();
-        while (it != currentIt) {
-            auto &m = (*it);
+        // By index: erasing from a Qt 6 QList invalidates the iterators after the erased element,
+        // so an iterator to the new (last) mode would be left dangling and the loop would run past
+        // the end. The new mode stays last.
+        for (qsizetype i = 0; i < modes.size() - 1;) {
+            auto &m = modes[i];
             if (m.flags.testFlag(Mode::Flag::Current)) {
                 m.flags &= ~Mode::Flags(Mode::Flag::Current);
                 Q_EMIT q->modeChanged(m);
             }
             if (m.refreshRate == mode.refreshRate && m.size == mode.size) {
-                it = modes.erase(it);
+                modes.removeAt(i);
                 existing = true;
             } else {
-                it++;
+                i++;
             }
         }
-        currentMode = *currentIt;
+        currentMode = modes.last();
     }
     if (existing) {
         Q_EMIT q->modeChanged(mode);
